{
  "commit_id": "5283d943d459564c7ac01b2e130fc46bdef5fcc8",
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Review Summary\n\n**Task:** @01KK6BECKPA5MHQAZJ2KNPEMP1\n**Spec:** @config-shadow\n\n### Own AC Coverage\n- [x] ac-11: pull-rebase before push is exercised in `tests/shadow.test.ts`\n- [x] ac-12: scheduler behavior is exercised in `tests/shadow-sync-scheduler.test.ts`\n\n### Trait AC Coverage\n- Repo-wide validation is noisy and not scoped to this task, so I relied on targeted review plus current CI.\n\n### Code Quality\n- **MUST-FIX:** the new daemon scheduler wiring introduces runtime-broken relative imports in the daemon bundle. This matches the current failing `e2e (playwright smoke)` check, where daemon startup times out on PR head.\n\n### Quality Gates\n- [x] Spec alignment reviewed\n- [x] Diff reviewed for AC-11 and AC-12\n- [ ] CI clean on current HEAD (`e2e (playwright smoke)` is failing)\n- [ ] Runtime startup regression cleared\n",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "packages/daemon/src/shadow-sync.ts",
      "line": 10,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: This relative import is not valid in the built daemon layout. `build:daemon` copies this file to `dist/daemon/shadow-sync.ts`, so `../../parser/shadow.js` resolves to `parser/shadow.js` at repo root instead of `dist/parser/shadow.js`. That makes daemon startup fail on the packaged/runtime path, which matches the red smoke CI."
    },
    {
      "path": "packages/daemon/src/server.ts",
      "line": 425,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: Same runtime path problem here. From `dist/daemon/server.ts`, `../../parser/config.js` resolves outside `dist`, so the daemon cannot load project config during startup. The current PR head already shows this as `e2e (playwright smoke)` failing with `Daemon failed to start within 5 seconds`."
    }
  ]
}
EOF

